NAME
       install - copy files and set their mode and owner in one step

SYNOPSIS
       install [OPTION]... SOURCE DEST
       install [OPTION]... SOURCE... DIRECTORY
       install -d [OPTION]... DIRECTORY...

DESCRIPTION
       install copies files like cp does, but also sets the permissions,
       owner and group of the copies in the same command. With -d it creates
       directories (and their parents) instead. Unless -m is given the new
       files and directories get mode 0755 (rwxr-xr-x), which suits programs
       and scripts.

OPTIONS
       -d, --directory
              Create the named directories, with any missing parents.

       -m, --mode=MODE
              Set this mode (octal, such as 640) instead of 0755.

       -o, --owner=USER
              Make USER the owner (only root may do this).

       -g, --group=GROUP
              Make GROUP the group.

       -v, --verbose
              Print the name of each file copied.

EXAMPLES
       Put a script in place, executable for everyone:
              # install -m 755 hello.sh /usr/local/bin/hello

       Create a directory owned by student, closed to others:
              # install -d -m 750 -o student -g student /srv/projects

SEE ALSO
       cp(1), mkdir(1), chmod(1), chown(1)
